<article class="env-lemma" id="0GJG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GJG">Lemma <span data-tag="0GJG">59.84.5</span>.</a> Let $\Lambda $ be a Noetherian ring, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, let $X$ be a separated finite type scheme over $k$ of dimension $\leq 1$, and let $0 \to \mathcal{F}_1 \to \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}_2 \to 0$ be a short exact sequence of sheaves of $\Lambda $-modules on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. If $H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F}_ i)$, $i = 1, 2$ are finite $\Lambda $-modules then $H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F})$ is a finite $\Lambda $-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from the long exact sequence of cohomology. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>